Z||000000||MooCow||09-18-2000||08:55 PM||||What is and where is it located?<BR>Someone told me that could be my problem when I go to take off.  On take of at times it grinds like metal hit the ground and dragged for like 2 seconds then nothing.  It does this in reverse and in 1st and when I started out in second it make the noise.  Anyone else have a clue to what it is?<BR>My car is a 86 Se V6 4-speed. <BR>Someone also said that it could be my flywheel dust cover.  Where is that located? As you can tell I am not really good with mechanical stuff but trying. <P>                              Thanks Ken||||reg||5
Z||000001||86SE||09-18-2000||09:24 PM||||Its the small 8" bar with 2 holes on either end.  It has a rubber bushing on each end, and is located at the bottom right hand side of the engine compartment.  It connects the engine to the chassis.<P>If the bushings look pretty torn up, or look loose, replace them.  Or just goto the Fiero Store and buy the "Ultimate Dog Bone" to replace it (poly bushings).<P>------------------<BR>'86 Special Edition,<BR>High-Output V-6 Yellow Fiero<BR>Special Rally Heavy Duty Suspention||||reg||1
Z||000002||Carrolles||09-19-2000||10:21 AM||||"Bottom Right Side" might sound confusing.  The strut is above the alternator at the right rear side of the engine (while standing at the back of the car looking forward) and connects to the front wall of the trunk.<P>There is another torque strut down low on the front right side of the engine underneath the A/C compressor.  It looks like a short Shock Absorber.||||reg||1
